# --- generated output: never hand-format, it is rewritten on every build -------------------------
# `dist/` and `declarations/` are rollup + `ember-tsc --declaration` output. Formatting them is
# pure churn (they revert on the next build) and they made up the bulk of the 243 files
# `prettier --check` was reporting repo-wide.
dist/
declarations/

# The addon's README.md and LICENSE.md are BUILD ARTIFACTS -- `rollup.config.mjs` copies them from
# the repo root on every build. Edit the root copies, never these. (Recorded in PORTING-NOTES.md.)
glide-data-grid-ember/README.md
glide-data-grid-ember/LICENSE.md

# Lockfile: generated by pnpm, which rewrites it in its own format anyway.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- upstream-derived code: NEVER format, to preserve diffability against the source repo --------
# `src/rendering/` is Phase 1's near-verbatim port of glide-data-grid's rendering engine (~7,160
# lines). This project's core workflow is diffing a ported file against its upstream counterpart at
# /Users/jxhui/Developer/glide-data-grid -- to confirm a port is faithful, to decide whether a
# surprising behaviour is an upstream bug to preserve or a port defect to fix, and to re-sync when
# upstream moves. Any reformatting breaks that comparison on every line.
#
# Ignoring is deliberately STRONGER than configuring prettier to match upstream's style: an ignored
# file cannot drift even if a future prettier version changes its output, and editors with
# format-on-save leave it alone. The trade-off is that these files get no formatting enforcement --
# that is the point. Their formatting is inherited from upstream and should stay that way.
glide-data-grid-ember/src/rendering/
# ...except our own test files, which live colocated in there but have no upstream counterpart.
!glide-data-grid-ember/src/rendering/**/*.test.ts

# Direct ports of upstream components, same reasoning.
glide-data-grid-ember/src/-private/growing-entry.ts
glide-data-grid-ember/src/-private/markdown-div.ts
